Ans 13- No, your local commit history did not change.
The git push command simply uploads a copy of your existing local commit history to the remote server (GitHub). Your local commits, hashes, and files remain exactly the same as they were before pushing.

Ans 14- A private repository securely exists on GitHub's servers. Its contents are fully accessible to the owner and explicitly invited collaborators (like your TAs), while remaining hidden from the general public.
